# Allowlist .gitignore (prove-it). Nothing is tracked unless admitted below.
# Why: a blocklist has to predict every shape a leak can take; an allowlist
# only has to know what this repo is for.
#
# To admit a new file or folder, APPEND one line at the end of this file, on
# purpose, when you first need it. Never use git add -f; the guard blocks it.
#   !/path/to/file.md      a single file at the root
#   !/folder/              a folder (and everything inside it)
/*
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/src/
# now-sdk project files (VERIFY against a real now-sdk init at your pinned version)
!/package.json
!/package-lock.json
!/now.config.json
!/tsconfig.json
!/now.dev.mjs
!/now.prebuild.mjs
!/.eslintrc

# Candidates (VERIFY against a real now-sdk init at your pinned version).
# To admit one, append its pattern line, uncommented, at the end of this file.
# editor workspace settings
# !/.vscode/
# CI workflows
# !/.github/
# licence file
# !/LICENSE
# newer ESLint config format
# !/eslint.config.mjs

# Process files — admit each when first created by APPENDING its line at the end of this file (never git add -f):
# the starter session protocol
# !/CLAUDE.md
# design records (docs/DESIGN-<Feature>.md), from the first design-challenge
# !/docs/
# the backlog, from the first build-plan
# !/BACKLOG.md
# the session note, from the first session close
# !/SESSION-NOTE.md
# the grade report, from the first grade
# !/GRADE.md
# the runbook, from the first handoff
# !/RUNBOOK.md
# the handoff record, from the first handoff
# !/HANDOFF.md
# CONSULT.md stays in the workspace, outside the repo; it is never admitted.

# Never track, even inside admitted folders:
.env*
.DS_Store
*.local
dist/

# Admitted lines appended below this point.
